+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+The default selector compares a provided template name with a fixed set of
+lowercase suffixes. See `proposal.md` for the motivation and the specification
+for the required behavior.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Normalize a provided filename only for standard extension matching.
+- Verify every supported extension accepts a mixed-case suffix and existing
+  fallback cases are retained.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Changing custom autoescape callbacks or Jinja configuration overrides.
+- Expanding the set of default supported extensions.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Compare a lowercase form of a non-`None` filename with the existing suffix
+  set. This keeps the recognized extension list intact while making its casing
+  irrelevant. Alternative: enumerate uppercase variants, which is incomplete
+  and unnecessarily duplicative.
+- Test the selector directly. This isolates default policy behavior without
+  requiring template files for each casing variant.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Filename normalization affects more than the suffix] → It is used solely
+  for the existing suffix comparison; unsupported extensions still return
+  false.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+The behavior is backward-compatible and needs no migration. Reverting the
+single comparison restores the prior behavior.
