+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector only recognizes lowercase template
+extensions, causing HTML, XHTML, XML, and SVG templates with uppercase or
+mixed-case suffixes to render unescaped content.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Recognize Flask's standard autoescaped template extensions regardless of
+  filename case.
+- Preserve the existing default for unsupported extensions and unnamed
+  templates.
+- Cover mixed-case supported extensions and unchanged non-matching behavior
+  with tests.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `template-autoescape-selection`: Default template autoescaping behavior
+  based on template filename extensions.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affects Flask's default Jinja autoescape selection and its templating tests.
+- No configuration, dependency, or public API changes are required.
