+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines predictable default escaping for supported template types regardless
+of the capitalization used in their filenames.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Case-insensitive standard template extension recognition
+The default template autoescape behavior SHALL enable autoescaping for template
+filenames ending in `.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`, or `.svg` regardless of
+the case of the extension characters.
+
+#### Scenario: Mixed-case supported extension
+- **WHEN** a template filename ends in a mixed-case variant of a supported
+  extension
+- **THEN** the default autoescape behavior is enabled
+
+#### Scenario: Unsupported or unnamed template
+- **WHEN** a template filename has no supported extension or no filename is
+  provided
+- **THEN** the default behavior remains unchanged: unsupported filenames are
+  not autoescaped and unnamed templates are autoescaped
